Extract and audit Android OTA/ROM images

Usage: android-doctor [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  extract     Extract partition images from an OTA zip or directory
  info        Print build info from an OTA without extracting
  amlogic     Describe an Amlogic image container (dt.img, dtbo.img, aml_upgrade_package.img)
  dt          Show a device tree, dtbo table, or an opaque container header
  fec         dm-verity forward error correction: generate Reed-Solomon parity for a file, verify a file against it, repair a damaged file
  verify-ota  Verify an OTA's signatures: the zip's whole-file (signapk) signature and the payload's metadata and payload signatures
  dex         Show the DEX files of an APK (or one .dex): header, tables, classes, methods, fields, strings, references, code
  apk         Audit one APK file: manifest, package, version, signers, code, issues
  apkcompare  Compare two builds of one APK: sizes, added, removed and changed entries, uses-feature changes and a patch-size estimate (no download size)
  partitions  Show a flash manifest (Qualcomm rawprogram*.xml or MediaTek scatter.txt) and check it against the image files actually present
  unpack      Show a boot or vendor_boot image's header, and with -o write its kernel, ramdisk, dtb, ...
  journal     Show the jbd2 journal of an ext3/ext4 image: superblock fields, clean/dirty status, and the transactions found by walking from `s_first`. Read-only: the image is never modified
  fsck        Cross-check an ext2/3/4 image superblock, group descriptors and allocation bitmaps (e2fsck-class), read-only
  ls          List a directory (or show one file) inside an ext2/3/4, erofs or f2fs image, without extracting it
  cat         Print one regular file from an ext2/3/4, erofs or f2fs image to standard output
  tree        Show the whole tree (or a subtree) of an ext2/3/4, erofs or f2fs image, recursively, without extracting it
  find        Find files in an ext2/3/4, erofs or f2fs image by name glob, SELinux label, setuid or setgid bit, extended attribute or content (read-only)
  stat        Show one path's metadata (type, inode, mode, owner, size, links, mtime, link target, xattrs and SELinux label) inside an ext2/3/4, erofs or f2fs image, without extracting it; symlinks are not followed
  prop        Print every value of one property from the image's property files (build.prop, default.prop, ...), with the file that sets it
  blocks      List the physical block numbers holding the data of one regular file inside an ext2/3/4 or f2fs image (holes are skipped; erofs is refused)
  icheck      Name the regular file that owns each physical block number inside an ext2/3/4 or f2fs image (blocks no file uses print as none)
  ncheck      Name the path or paths of each inode number inside an ext2/3/4, erofs or f2fs image (inodes with no path print as none)
  init        Decode one init service (`service <name>` block) from the image's .rc files: path, args, user, groups, capabilities, sockets
  deleted     List deleted inodes in an ext2/3/4 image (like debugfs lsdel) and optionally recover their data
  audit       Security posture of firmware images: ADB properties, setuid files, su binaries, init services
  diff        Compare two firmware builds file by file: added, removed and modified files (by SHA-256), mode, owner, capability and SELinux-label changes, property and init-service changes; what got worse becomes findings
  avbmake     Write a new vbmeta image (avbtool make_vbmeta_image without descriptors): header, SHA-256 digest and RSA signature
  avbfooter   Write a copy of a partition image with an AVB hash footer (avbtool add_hash_footer): the image, a vbmeta with one SHA-256 hash descriptor and the footer, padded to --partition-size. The input is never modified
  avberase    Write a copy of a partition image without its AVB footer and vbmeta (avbtool erase_footer)
  avbkey      Write the AVB public key blob of a PEM RSA key (avbtool extract_public_key) and print its SHA-256 digest
  avbkeygen   Generate an RSA private key as a PKCS#1 PEM file (avbtool gen_key); prints only the public key digest
  vbkernel    Verify a ChromeOS kernel partition (vboot 2.x): keyblock, kernel preamble and body signatures
  vbsign      Re-sign a ChromeOS kernel partition (vboot 2.x): the data key replaces the data key in the keyblock and signs the preamble and body, the root key signs the keyblock; the output is verified before it is written
  avbcert     Build AVB certificate files (avb_cert): avbtool make_certificate, make_cert_permanent_attributes, make_cert_metadata, make_cert_unlock_credential
  vbmeta      Show an AVB vbmeta image (or a partition with an AVB footer): header, key, signature, descriptors, hashes
  ramdisk     List a boot image's ramdisk (or a ramdisk file), report its ADB properties, and with -o extract it
  files       List or extract the files of an ext2/3/4, erofs or f2fs image (with SELinux labels), no root needed
  sparse      Turn a raw image into an Android sparse image
  mkbootimg   Build a boot image (header versions 0 to 2) from its sections; the inverse of unpacking one
  unsparse    Turn Android sparse image(s) into a raw image
  identify    Say what each file is, by its magic bytes (never by name)
  report      Staleness verdict from the OTA's build metadata
  hash-tree   Regenerate the dm-verity hash tree for a partition image rebuilt from a payload
  doctor      Run a deterministic health scan on an unpacked firmware directory
  fix         Scan, then hand the findings to a coding agent as one fix prompt
  ci          CI integration: write a GitHub Actions workflow that runs the android-doctor action
  mcp         Expose android-doctor over the Model Context Protocol (JSON-RPC on stdio)
  shell       Browse the findings of a firmware directory or image in an interactive shell
  explore     Browse the findings of a firmware directory or image in a full-screen explorer
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --no-color  Never emit colour, even on a terminal (also honours the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -h, --help      Print help
  -V, --version   Print version
